%20is%20removed.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27existingAgentWorkConcludesGradually%27%2C%20%27coordinatorWorksAloneAfterAgentCompletion%27%2C%20%27inheritedProjectScopeRetained%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%5D%2C%20true%29%2C%0A%20%20...rows%28%27associativeDataStorageRequest%27%2C%20associativeDataSource%2C%20%27associative-data-storage%27%2C%20%27associative-data-storage%27%2C%20%5B%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-ASSOCIATIVE-DATA-STORAGE%27%2C%20%27project-owned%20structured%20data%20stored%20through%20the%20associative%20Links%20stack%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Project-owned%20structured%20records%2C%20including%20native%20grammar%20corpus%20fixtures%20such%20as%20the%20Agda%20corpus%2C%20use%20inspectable%20Links%20Notation%20through%20the%20relevant%20associative%20stack%20by%20default.%20Generated%20native%20grammars%2C%20fixture%20records%20and%20shared%20package%20data%20remain%20reconstructable%20and%20usable%20through%20the%20existing%20public%20algorithms%20without%20hidden%20authoritative%20JSON%20side%20tables.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27projectStructuredDataUsesLinksNotation%27%2C%20%27nativeGrammarCorpusStoredAsLinkedRecords%27%2C%20%27associativeStackDataAlgorithmsReused%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-ASSOCIATIVE-DATA-AUTOMATED-CONVERSION%27%2C%20%27automated%20lossless%20conversion%20of%20structured%20data%20and%20fixture%20metadata%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Structured-data%20migration%20is%20automated%20rather%20than%20manually%20rewriting%20records.%20The%20converter%20losslessly%20reconstructs%20the%20original%20values%20and%20preserves%20identities%2C%20source%20order%2C%20exact%20numbers%2C%20strings%2C%20aliases%2C%20required%20fixtures%2C%20acceptance%20assertions%20and%20cross-record%20references.%20Both%20package%20readers%20and%20repository%20tooling%20retain%20their%20observable%20behavior%2C%20and%20conversion%20does%20not%20reduce%20protected%20requirement%20scope.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27structuredDataConversionAutomated%27%2C%20%27convertedValuesLosslesslyReconstructed%27%2C%20%27identitiesOrderNumbersStringsAliasesAndReferencesPreserved%27%2C%20%27fixtureIdsAndAcceptanceAssertionsPreserved%27%2C%20%27packageReadersAndToolingBehaviorPreserved%27%2C%20%27protectedScopeNotReduced%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-ASSOCIATIVE-DATA-JSON-EXCEPTIONS%27%2C%20%27JSON%20retained%20only%20for%20necessary%20declared%20external%20interfaces%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27JSON%20remains%20only%20where%20a%20genuine%20external%20standard%20or%20source-language%20JSON%20interface%20requires%20it%2C%20with%20an%20explicit%20recorded%20necessity%20and%20boundary.%20Convenience%2C%20an%20existing%20JSON%20file%20or%20an%20opaque%20payload%20does%20not%20establish%20an%20exception%3B%20the%20project-owned%20authoritative%20representation%20remains%20linked%20data%20wherever%20the%20interface%20permits%20it.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27jsonExceptionsHaveExplicitNecessity%27%2C%20%27externalJsonInterfaceBoundariesRecorded%27%2C%20%27noConvenienceOrOpaquePayloadException%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%5D%2C%20true%29%2C%0A%20%20...rows%28%27externalGrammarStorageRequest%27%2C%20externalGrammarSource%2C%20%27temporary-external-grammar-inputs%27%2C%20%27external-grammar-storage%27%2C%20%5B%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-EXTERNAL-GRAMMAR-UNTRACKED%27%2C%20%27upstream%20external%20grammar%20and%20parser%20assets%20excluded%20from%20version%20control%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Upstream%20external%20raw%20grammars%2C%20parser%20sources%2C%20compiled%20parsers%20and%20WebAssembly%20assets%20are%20not%20tracked%20in%20the%20repository.%20The%20project-generated%20native%20or%20meta-language%20Links%20Notation%20grammars%20and%20prepared%20snapshots%20remain%20permitted%20and%20preserve%20all%20inherited%20grammar%2C%20provenance%20and%20offline%20production%20requirements.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27externalUpstreamAssetsUntracked%27%2C%20%27generatedNativeSnapshotsRetained%27%2C%20%27inheritedOfflineAndProvenanceRequirementsPreserved%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-EXTERNAL-GRAMMAR-TEMPORARY-DOWNLOAD%27%2C%20%27temporary%20pinned%20external%20grammar%20inputs%20with%20checked%20provenance%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27A%20reproducible%20tool%20downloads%20upstream%20external%20grammar%20and%20oracle%20assets%20temporarily%20when%20import%2C%20regeneration%20or%20independent%20tests%20require%20them%2C%20verifies%20their%20pinned%20checksums%20and%20records%20revision%2C%20origin%20and%20license%20provenance.%20Downloaded%20inputs%20remain%20outside%20tracked%20files%2C%20temporary%20assets%20are%20cleaned%20after%20use%2C%20and%20generated%20native%20snapshots%20remain%20independently%20usable%20without%20those%20assets.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27temporaryDownloaderExecuted%27%2C%20%27pinnedChecksumsVerified%27%2C%20%27downloadProvenanceRetained%27%2C%20%27downloadedAssetsUntracked%27%2C%20%27temporaryAssetsCleaned%27%2C%20%27generatedSnapshotsUsableWithoutDownloads%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%5D%2C%20true%29%2C%0A%20%20...rows%28%27externalGrammarIgnoreRequest%27%2C%20externalGrammarIgnoreSource%2C%20%27temporary-external-grammar-inputs%27%2C%20%27external-grammar-storage%27%2C%20%5B%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-EXTERNAL-GRAMMAR-IGNORED-DIRECTORY%27%2C%20%27external%20grammar%20download%20folders%20explicitly%20ignored%20by%20Git%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Every%20folder%20used%20for%20external%20grammar%2C%20parser%20or%20oracle%20downloads%20is%20explicitly%20covered%20by%20Git%20ignore%20rules%2C%20so%20ordinary%20staging%20cannot%20add%20downloaded%20inputs.%20Ignore%20rules%20preserve%20the%20project-generated%20native%20Links%20Notation%20grammars%2C%20source%20manifests%2C%20checksums%20and%20provenance%20records%20that%20must%20remain%20tracked.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27externalGrammarDirectoriesIgnored%27%2C%20%27ordinaryStagingExcludesDownloads%27%2C%20%27generatedSnapshotsAndProvenanceRemainTracked%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%5D%2C%20true%29%2C%0A%20%20...rows%28%27grammarInferenceIssue%27%2C%20inferenceSource%2C%20%27dynamic-knowledge-and-language-extension%27%2C%20%27grammar-inference%27%2C%20%5B%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-GRAMMAR-INFERENCE-EXISTING-WORK-AUDIT%27%2C%20%27existing%20inference%20foundations%20and%20JavaScript%20parity%20gaps%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Audit%20and%20reuse%20the%20lexical%2C%20state-merging%2C%20context-free%2C%20structural-prior%2C%20active-learning%20and%20minimization%20work%20associated%20with%20issues93%2C114%2C117%20through123%20and%20the%20existing%20Rust%20inference%20modules.%20Closed%20issues%20do%20not%20prove%20complete%20capability%20or%20remove%20JavaScript%20parity%20obligations.%27%2C%20%5B%27existingInferenceModulesAudited%27%2C%20%27closedIssueEvidenceRechecked%27%2C%20%27javascriptParityGapsRecorded%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-GRAMMAR-INFERENCE-RESEARCH-SELECTION%27%2C%20%27pinned%20modern%20grammar%20discovery%20research%20and%20selection%20rationale%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Compare%20the%20pinned%20XVada%2C%20Crucio%2C%20NatGI%20and%20attributed%20grammar-inference%20methods%20with%20recorded%20revisions%2C%20implementations%2C%20licenses%2C%20independent%20oracles%2C%20datasets%20and%20configurations.%20Paper-reported%20results%20remain%20hypotheses%20for%20local%20reproduction%2C%20and%20method%20selection%20retains%20its%20evidence%20rationale.%27%2C%20%5B%27researchRevisionsAndLicensesPinned%27%2C%20%27fourResearchMethodsEvaluated%27%2C%20%27selectionRationaleAndReproductionRecorded%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-GRAMMAR-INFERENCE-INDEPENDENT-EVALUATION%27%2C%20%27independent%20held-out%20grammar%20discovery%20evaluation%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Separate%20discovery%20training%20from%20holdout%20evaluation%20and%20test%20adversarial%20rejections%20and%20real%20projects%20under%20several%20independent%20oracles.%20Record%20precision%2C%20recall%2C%20F1%2C%20CST%20fields%2C%20trivia%2C%20spans%2C%20attributed%20behavior%2C%20reconstruction%2C%20grammar%20size%2C%20determinism%2C%20query%20counts%2C%20elapsed%20time%20and%20peak%20memory.%27%2C%20%5B%27trainingAndHoldoutSeparated%27%2C%20%27multipleIndependentOraclesAndProjectsUsed%27%2C%20%27allRequiredQualityAndResourceMetricsRecorded%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-GRAMMAR-INFERENCE-COMPARATIVE-BENCHMARKS%27%2C%20%27reproducible%20inference%20comparison%20within%20common%20budgets%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Benchmark%20existing%20inference%20and%20selected%20modern%20methods%20with%20the%20same%20pinned%20workloads%20and%20budgets.%20Retain%20all%20failures%20and%20disagreement%20traces%2C%20select%20reproducible%20improvements%20without%20weakening%20acceptance%2C%20and%20keep%20statistical%20coverage%20distinct%20from%20semantic%20proof.%27%2C%20%5B%27commonBudgetsAndWorkloadsUsed%27%2C%20%27failuresAndDisagreementsRetained%27%2C%20%27reproducibleImprovementMeasured%27%2C%20%27statisticsNotPresentedAsProof%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-GRAMMAR-INFERENCE-CI-RESOURCE-POLICY%27%2C%20%27bounded%20JavaScript-first%20inference%20development%20and%20CI%20artifacts%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Use%20targeted%20JavaScript%20authoring%20locally%3B%20run%20Rust%20compilation%2C%20broad%20discovery%20experiments%2C%20whole%20corpora%20and%20downstream%20workloads%20in%20CI%20with%20bounded%20caches%20and%20per-run%20artifacts.%20Record%20critical%20scope%2C%20API%20parity%20and%20exact%20executed%20observations%20without%20completion%20claims%20for%20missing%20behavior.%27%2C%20%5B%27javascriptFirstInferenceDevelopment%27%2C%20%27expensiveInferenceAndRustRunInCI%27%2C%20%27boundedCachesAndRunArtifacts%27%2C%20%27exactEvidenceAndApiParityRecorded%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%5D%2C%20true%29%2C%0A%20%20...rows%28%27grammarInferenceIssue%27%2C%20inferenceSource%2C%20%27dynamic-knowledge-and-language-extension%27%2C%20%27grammar-inference%27%2C%20%5B%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-GRAMMAR-INFERENCE-PUBLIC-API-CLI%27%2C%20%27matching%20public%20grammar%20discovery%20library%20and%20CLI%20interfaces%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27JavaScript%20and%20Rust%20library%20and%20CLI%20interfaces%20accept%20pinned%20positive%20and%20negative%20examples%2C%20independent%20membership%20or%20parser%20oracles%2C%20optional%20execution%20traces%20and%20existing%20grammars.%20Diagnostics%20identify%20unresolved%20context%20sensitivity%2C%20scanners%20and%20action%20semantics%20rather%20than%20silently%20approximating%20them.%27%2C%20%5B%27matchingDiscoveryApiAndCliExecuted%27%2C%20%27examplesOraclesTracesAndSourcesAccepted%27%2C%20%27unsupportedSemanticsPreciselyDiagnosed%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-GRAMMAR-INFERENCE-NATIVE-OUTPUT%27%2C%20%27fully%20native%20executable%20discovered%20grammars%20and%20attributed%20behavior%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Discovery%20emits%20executable%20Links%20grammars%20with%20lossless%20CST%20structure%2C%20lexer%20and%20scanner%20state%2C%20precedence%2C%20ambiguity%2C%20recovery%20and%20attributed%20semantic%20actions.%20Foreign%20parser%20blobs%2C%20opaque%20sources%20and%20host%20callbacks%20cannot%20stand%20in%20for%20native%20operational%20definitions.%27%2C%20%5B%27discoveredGrammarNativeAndExecutable%27%2C%20%27discoveredCstAndScannerSemanticsPreserved%27%2C%20%27attributedActionsAndRecoveryExplicit%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-GRAMMAR-INFERENCE-GENERIC-UNION%27%2C%20%27generic%20structural%20and%20semantic%20discovery%20through%20the%20source-union%20pipeline%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Discover%20lexical%20classes%2C%20recursion%20and%20semantic%20relations%20generically%2C%20preserving%20every%20source%20production%20and%20provenance.%20Merge%20discovered%20definitions%20with%20the%20applicable%20official%20and%20mature%20grammars%20through%20the%20existing%20automatic%20native%20pipeline.%27%2C%20%5B%27lexicalRecursiveAndSemanticDiscoveryExecuted%27%2C%20%27allSourceProductionsAndProvenanceRetained%27%2C%20%27discoveredAndOfficialGrammarsMerged%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-GRAMMAR-INFERENCE-FORMAL-CONCEPT-INTEGRATION%27%2C%20%27discovered%20concepts%20integrated%20with%20recursive%20formal%20definitions%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Copy%20discovered%20concepts%20into%20the%20single%20global%20space%20with%20formal%20definitions%20that%20recursively%20reference%20other%20linked%20concepts.%20Deduplicate%20only%20checked%20context-preserving%20one-to-one%20meaning%20certificates%3B%20equal%20strings%2C%20names%2C%20glosses%20or%20finite%20samples%20do%20not%20establish%20equivalence%2C%20and%20unresolved%20alternatives%20survive.%27%2C%20%5B%27discoveredConceptsAndFormalDefinitionsLinked%27%2C%20%27contextPreservingMeaningCertificatesChecked%27%2C%20%27unresolvedDiscoveryAlternativesPreserved%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-GRAMMAR-INFERENCE-DETERMINISTIC-REFINEMENT%27%2C%20%27deterministic%20counterexample-guided%20incremental%20discovery%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Seeded%20discovery%20is%20deterministic%20and%20supports%20counterexample-guided%20refinement%2C%20incremental%20updates%20and%20checkpoint%20resume%20without%20losing%20the%20examples%2C%20decisions%2C%20assumptions%20or%20rejected%20alternatives%20used%20to%20obtain%20the%20grammar.%27%2C%20%5B%27seededDiscoveryDeterministic%27%2C%20%27counterexampleAndIncrementalRefinementExecuted%27%2C%20%27checkpointResumeRetainsEvidence%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-GRAMMAR-INFERENCE-SOURCE-FREE-SNAPSHOTS%27%2C%20%27source-free%20discovered%20grammar%20snapshots%20in%20text%20and%20versioned%20binary%20links%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Discovered%20snapshots%20restore%20and%20extend%20through%20link-cli%2C%20text%20Links%20Notation%20and%20a%20versioned%20binary%20links%20representation%20without%20their%20original%20source%20buffers%2C%20retaining%20identities%2C%20cycles%2C%20roots%2C%20full%20CSTs%20and%20proofs.%27%2C%20%5B%27discoverySnapshotsReloadWithoutSource%27%2C%20%27linkCliTextAndVersionedBinaryAgree%27%2C%20%27snapshotIdentitiesRootsTreesAndProofsRetained%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-GRAMMAR-INFERENCE-DYNAMIC-TRANSLATION%27%2C%20%27discovered%20languages%20execute%20and%20translate%20in%20the%20generic%20runtime%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27After%20installing%20a%20discovered%20language%20dynamically%2C%20ordinary%20parsing%20and%20Rust%2FJavaScript%20translation%20execute%20through%20the%20common%20algorithms.%20Changing%20a%20linked%20definition%20changes%20execution%20without%20changing%20the%20generic%20host%20runtime%3B%20stale%20certificates%20and%20incompatible%20definitions%20are%20rejected%20or%20revalidated%20explicitly.%27%2C%20%5B%27discoveredLanguageParsesAndTranslates%27%2C%20%27linkedMutationChangesGenericExecution%27%2C%20%27staleCertificatesRejectedOrRevalidated%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%5D%29%2C%0A%20%20...rows%28%27dynamicKnowledgeRequest%27%2C%20dynamicSource%2C%20%27dynamic-knowledge-and-language-extension%27%2C%20%27dynamic-knowledge%27%2C%20%5B%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-KNOWLEDGE-RDF-SUPPORT%27%2C%20%27full%20Resource%20Description%20Framework%20representation%20and%20operations%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Both%20packages%20preserve%20the%20complete%20required%20RDF%20constructs%2C%20identities%2C%20relationships%2C%20literals%2C%20provenance%20and%20selected%20semantics%20as%20inspectable%20links.%20A%20finite%20triple%20example%20or%20opaque%20payload%20does%20not%20establish%20full%20RDF%20support.%27%2C%20%5B%27rdfConstructsPreserved%27%2C%20%27rdfSemanticsAndProvenanceExplicit%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-KNOWLEDGE-OWL-SUPPORT%27%2C%20%27full%20Web%20Ontology%20Language%20representation%20and%20operations%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Both%20packages%20represent%20the%20required%20OWL%20constructs%2C%20formal%20axioms%20and%20chosen%20semantic%20profiles%20as%20links%2C%20preserving%20distinctions%20and%20obligations%20without%20silently%20replacing%20the%20consumer%20foundation.%27%2C%20%5B%27owlConstructsAndAxiomsPreserved%27%2C%20%27owlSemanticProfilesExplicit%27%2C%20%27consumerFoundationRetained%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-KNOWLEDGE-RDF-OWL-IMPORT%27%2C%20%27complete%20RDF%20and%20OWL%20importers%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Public%20importers%20in%20both%20packages%20import%20required%20RDF%20and%20OWL%20representations%20into%20the%20common%20concept%20and%20links%20space%20with%20their%20full%20structure%2C%20provenance%20and%20explicit%20diagnostics%20for%20unresolved%20obligations.%27%2C%20%5B%27rdfAndOwlPublicImportersExecuted%27%2C%20%27importedKnowledgeStructureAndProvenanceRetained%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-KNOWLEDGE-RDF-OWL-CONVERSION%27%2C%20%27faithful%20RDF%20and%20OWL%20conversion%20cycles%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Public%20converters%20and%20exporters%20in%20both%20packages%20execute%20faithful%20knowledge-format%20conversion%20cycles%20from%20the%20shared%20representation%20without%20returning%20a%20saved%20input%20or%20silently%20weakening%20axioms%20and%20identities.%27%2C%20%5B%27knowledgeConversionCyclesExecuted%27%2C%20%27knowledgeAxiomsAndIdentitiesPreserved%27%2C%20%27noSavedInputConversionShortcut%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-KNOWLEDGE-RDF-OWL-MERGE%27%2C%20%27meaning-preserving%20RDF%20and%20OWL%20merges%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Both%20packages%20merge%20imported%20RDF%20and%20OWL%20knowledge%20through%20the%20common%20links%20space%2C%20deduplicating%20only%20proved%20correspondences%20while%20retaining%20unique%20concepts%2C%20conflicting%20axioms%2C%20uncertainty%20and%20source-qualified%20provenance.%27%2C%20%5B%27knowledgeMergesExecuted%27%2C%20%27knowledgeDeduplicationProved%27%2C%20%27conflictsAndUncertaintyPreserved%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-DYNAMIC-SNAPSHOT-RECONSTRUCTION%27%2C%20%27static%20snapshot%20becomes%20a%20complete%20dynamic%20representation%20on%20demand%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27A%20prepared%20static%20snapshot%20can%20be%20reconstructed%20on%20demand%20into%20the%20complete%20CST%20and%20concept%20space%2C%20retaining%20rules%2C%20formal%20definitions%2C%20identities%2C%20recursive%20links%2C%20source%20bytes%20and%20provenance%20instead%20of%20reconstructing%20a%20token%20list%20or%20descriptor.%27%2C%20%5B%27snapshotReconstructsFullCst%27%2C%20%27snapshotReconstructsFullConceptSpace%27%2C%20%27dynamicReconstructionRetainsProvenance%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-DYNAMIC-RECONSTRUCTION-RESOURCE-MEASUREMENT%27%2C%20%27measured%20latency%20and%20resources%20for%20complete%20dynamic%20reconstruction%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Both%20packages%20measure%20actual%20complete%20CST%20and%20concept-space%20reconstruction%20through%20the%20public%20link-cli%2C%20text%20Links%20Notation%20and%20binary%20Links%20Notation%20paths.%20Measurements%20record%20reconstruction%20latency%20and%20peak%20resources%20together%20with%20pinned%20input%20identity%2C%20representation%2C%20size%2C%20algorithm%20and%20execution%20environment%20provenance.%20The%20reconstructed%20graphs%20preserve%20the%20complete%20trees%2C%20rules%2C%20recursive%20formal%20definitions%2C%20identities%2C%20references%2C%20selected%20models%2C%20source%20bytes%20and%20provenance.%20Lazy%20loading%2C%20token-only%20reconstruction%20and%20descriptor%20creation%20cannot%20count%20as%20a%20measured%20full%20rebuild.%20These%20measurements%20retain%20the%20source%20qualitative%20speed%20requirement%20without%20inventing%20a%20numeric%20deadline.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27completeDynamicReconstructionMeasured%27%2C%20%27reconstructionLatencyAndResourcesRecorded%27%2C%20%27measurementInputAndEnvironmentProvenanceRetained%27%2C%20%27fullRepresentationPreservationRetained%27%2C%20%27lazyOrTokenOnlyReconstructionNotCounted%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-DYNAMIC-LINK-CLI-RECONSTRUCTION%27%2C%20%27dynamic%20reconstruction%20through%20link-cli%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27The%20dynamic%20representation%20can%20be%20recreated%20and%20processed%20through%20link-cli%20with%20a%20reproducible%20public%20path%2C%20preserving%20the%20complete%20trees%2C%20concept%20definitions%20and%20selected%20model.%27%2C%20%5B%27linkCliReconstructionExecuted%27%2C%20%27linkCliPreservesFullTreesAndConcepts%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-DYNAMIC-TEXT-LINKS-RECONSTRUCTION%27%2C%20%27dynamic%20reconstruction%20from%20text%20Links%20Notation%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Text%20Links%20Notation%20can%20serialize%2C%20reload%20and%20extend%20the%20complete%20dynamic%20CST%20and%20concept%20space%20without%20the%20original%20grammar%20or%20source%20buffers.%27%2C%20%5B%27textLinksDynamicRoundTripExecuted%27%2C%20%27textLinksPreservesCompleteRepresentation%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-DYNAMIC-BINARY-LINKS-RECONSTRUCTION%27%2C%20%27dynamic%20reconstruction%20from%20binary%20Links%20Notation%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Binary%20Links%20Notation%20can%20serialize%2C%20reload%20and%20extend%20the%20same%20complete%20dynamic%20representation%20with%20parity%20to%20its%20text%20form%20and%20without%20hidden%20authoritative%20side%20tables.%27%2C%20%5B%27binaryLinksDynamicRoundTripExecuted%27%2C%20%27textAndBinaryDynamicRepresentationsAgree%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-DYNAMIC-LANGUAGE-EXTENSION%27%2C%20%27algorithmic%20runtime%20extension%20with%20other%20languages%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Users%20can%20apply%20the%20shared%20algorithms%20to%20extend%20the%20dynamic%20meta-language%20with%20new%20languages%2C%20grammars%20and%20formal%20concepts.%20Extensions%20retain%20the%20global%20concept%20space%2C%20validation%2C%20source%20provenance%20and%20default%20behavior%20of%20existing%20catalog%20languages.%27%2C%20%5B%27dynamicLanguageExtensionExecuted%27%2C%20%27extensionUsesSharedAlgorithms%27%2C%20%27existingLanguageBehaviorPreserved%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%5D%29%2C%0A%20%20...rows%28%27dynamicKnowledgeRequest%27%2C%20dynamicSource%2C%20%27dynamic-knowledge-and-language-extension%27%2C%20%27grammar-inference%27%2C%20%5B%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-GRAMMAR-INFERENCE-SEPARATE-ISSUE%27%2C%20%27separate%20tracked%20automatic%20grammar%20inference%20issue%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27A%20separate%20repository%20issue%20records%20automatic%20grammar%20inference%20and%20discovery%20with%20modern%20primary%20research%2C%20concrete%20algorithm%20obligations%2C%20source%20provenance%2C%20behavioral%20acceptance%20and%20links%20back%20to%20this%20critical%20scope.%20Creating%20the%20issue%20does%20not%20satisfy%20inference%20implementation.%27%2C%20%5B%27separateInferenceIssueCreated%27%2C%20%27modernResearchAndAcceptanceRecorded%27%2C%20%27issueDoesNotSubstituteImplementation%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%5D%2C%20true%29%2C%0A%20%20...rows%28%27dynamicKnowledgeRequest%27%2C%20dynamicSource%2C%20%27dynamic-knowledge-and-language-extension%27%2C%20%27grammar-inference%27%2C%20%5B%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-GRAMMAR-INFERENCE-AUTOMATIC-DISCOVERY%27%2C%20%27automatic%20grammar%20inference%20through%20research-backed%20algorithms%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Both%20packages%20discover%20or%20infer%20grammar%20definitions%20using%20recorded%20modern%20research%20and%20explicit%20assumptions%2C%20then%20validate%20and%20integrate%20the%20inferred%20definitions%20through%20the%20native%20pipeline%20and%20concept%20space%20with%20independent%20accepted%20and%20rejected%20observations.%27%2C%20%5B%27automaticGrammarDiscoveryExecuted%27%2C%20%27researchAndAssumptionsPinned%27%2C%20%27inferredGrammarsIndependentlyValidated%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%5D%29%2C%0A%20%20...rows%28%27translationPriorityRequest%27%2C%20translationSource%2C%20%27critical-conversation-requirements%27%2C%20%27translation-priority%27%2C%20%5B%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-TRANSLATION-PRIORITY-RUST%27%2C%20%27immediate%20bidirectional%20Rust%20and%20meta-language%20translation%20priority%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Current%20implementation%20priority%20maximizes%20Rust%20to%20editable%20meta-language%20and%20meta-language%20to%20Rust%20translation%2C%20including%20complete%20source%20and%20semantic%20preservation%20obligations.%20Earlier%20languages%2C%20knowledge-format%20support%20and%20inherited%20requirements%20remain%20in%20scope.%27%2C%20%5B%27rustToMetaLanguageExecuted%27%2C%20%27metaLanguageToRustExecuted%27%2C%20%27rustPriorityPreservesInheritedScope%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-TRANSLATION-PRIORITY-JAVASCRIPT%27%2C%20%27immediate%20bidirectional%20JavaScript%20and%20meta-language%20translation%20priority%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Current%20implementation%20priority%20maximizes%20JavaScript%20to%20editable%20meta-language%20and%20meta-language%20to%20JavaScript%20translation%2C%20retaining%20complete%20source%2C%20structures%20and%20semantics%20while%20preserving%20every%20earlier%20requirement.%27%2C%20%5B%27javascriptToMetaLanguageExecuted%27%2C%20%27metaLanguageToJavascriptExecuted%27%2C%20%27javascriptPriorityPreservesInheritedScope%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%5D%29%2C%0A%20%20...rows%28%27multiProjectTranslationRequest%27%2C%20projectSource%2C%20%27critical-conversation-requirements%27%2C%20%27translation-priority%27%2C%20%5B%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-TRANSLATION-PRIORITY-MULTI-PROJECT%27%2C%20%27reusable%20source%20translation%20across%20multiple%20JavaScript%20and%20Rust%20projects%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27The%20same%20automated%20translation%20and%20common%20concept%20algorithms%20operate%20on%20multiple%20real%20JavaScript%20and%20Rust%20projects%20with%20pinned%20inputs%20and%20independent%20behavioral%20validation.%20Project-specific%20source%20rewrites%20or%20carried%20originals%20do%20not%20establish%20successful%20reusable%20executable%20translation.%27%2C%20%5B%27multipleRealProjectsTranslated%27%2C%20%27sharedTranslationAlgorithmsReused%27%2C%20%27projectBehaviorsIndependentlyValidated%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%5D%29%2C%0A%20%20...rows%28%27recursiveDefinitionsRequest%27%2C%20definitionSource%2C%20%27recursive-formal-concept-definitions%27%2C%20%27formal-concept-definitions%27%2C%20%5B%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-FORMAL-CONCEPT-DEFINITIONS%27%2C%20%27deep%20formal%20definition%20of%20every%20concept%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Every%20concept%20has%20a%20recursively%20inspectable%20formal%20definition%20represented%20as%20links%2C%20with%20explicit%20axioms%2C%20operations%2C%20bindings%20and%20declared%20foundational%20primitives.%20An%20English%20description%20or%20opaque%20semantic%20signature%20is%20insufficient%20as%20its%20formal%20definition.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27everyConceptFormallyDefined%27%2C%20%27definitionsAreInspectableLinks%27%2C%20%27foundationalPrimitivesExplicit%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-FORMAL-CONCEPT-REFERENCES%27%2C%20%27mutual%20references%20between%20formal%20concept%20definitions%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Concept%20definitions%20can%20use%20other%20concepts%20recursively%20while%20retaining%20stable%20identities%2C%20qualified%20references%20and%20the%20selected%20foundation.%20Shared%20and%20cyclic%20references%20serialize%20and%20reload%20without%20flattening%20definitions%20or%20discarding%20their%20assumptions.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27recursiveConceptReferencesPreserved%27%2C%20%27sharedAndCyclicDefinitionsReloaded%27%2C%20%27definitionAssumptionsPreserved%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-FORMAL-CONCEPT-MEANING-COMPARISON%27%2C%20%27formal%20definitions%20as%20evidence%20of%20equal%20concept%20meaning%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Meaning%20comparison%20uses%20the%20complete%20recursive%20formal%20definitions%20and%20checked%20obligations%20under%20their%20explicit%20foundations.%20Equal%20names%2C%20source%20text%2C%20labels%20or%20declared%20meaning%20signatures%20alone%20cannot%20certify%20semantic%20equivalence%3B%20unresolved%20obligations%20preserve%20separate%20concepts.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27formalDefinitionsCompared%27%2C%20%27semanticObligationsChecked%27%2C%20%27unprovedMeaningEquivalenceRejected%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%5D%29%2C%0A%20%20...rows%28%27recursiveDefinitionsRequest%27%2C%20definitionSource%2C%20%27ontology-and-taxonomy-entry-points%27%2C%20%27ontology-and-taxonomy%27%2C%20%5B%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-ONTOLOGY-LIBRARY-ENTRYPOINT%27%2C%20%27separate%20ontology%20library%20entry%20point%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Both%20packages%20expose%20a%20separate%20ontology%20entry%20point%20for%20concepts%2C%20relationships%20and%20formal%20axioms%20in%20the%20global%20space%2C%20including%20concepts%20unused%20by%20any%20language%20grammar.%20Their%20definitions%20and%20links%20remain%20available%20without%20caller%20grammar%20registration.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27ontologyEntryPointAvailable%27%2C%20%27grammarUnusedConceptsAvailable%27%2C%20%27ontologyDefinitionsAndRelationsInspectable%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-TAXONOMY-LIBRARY-ENTRYPOINT%27%2C%20%27separate%20taxonomy%20library%20entry%20point%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Both%20packages%20expose%20a%20separate%20taxonomy%20entry%20point%20for%20classification%20and%20explicitly%20declared%20subsumption%20links%20over%20the%20global%20concept%20space%2C%20including%20concepts%20unused%20by%20grammars.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27taxonomyEntryPointAvailable%27%2C%20%27classificationAndSubsumptionInspectable%27%2C%20%27grammarUnusedTaxonomyConceptsAvailable%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-ONTOLOGY-TAXONOMY-MEMBERSHIP%27%2C%20%27concept%20membership%20in%20ontology%2C%20taxonomy%20or%20both%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27A%20concept%20can%20occur%20in%20the%20ontology%2C%20taxonomy%20or%20both%20through%20the%20same%20global%20identity.%20Grammar%20reachability%20never%20removes%20a%20concept%2C%20and%20both%20entry%20points%20retain%20its%20recursive%20formal%20definition%20and%20provenance.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27sharedOntologyTaxonomyIdentity%27%2C%20%27membershipIndependentOfGrammarReachability%27%2C%20%27definitionsAndProvenanceRetained%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-ONTOLOGY-TAXONOMY-RELATION-DISTINCTION%27%2C%20%27distinction%20between%20general%20relations%20and%20classification%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27The%20ontology%20represents%20concepts%2C%20relationships%20and%20formal%20axioms%3B%20the%20taxonomy%20represents%20classification%20or%20declared%20subsumption.%20An%20arbitrary%20associative%20relation%20does%20not%20become%20a%20classification%20edge%2C%20and%20the%20chosen%20hierarchy%20semantics%20remain%20explicit%20links.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27ontologyAndTaxonomyRolesDistinct%27%2C%20%27arbitraryRelationsDoNotImplyClassification%27%2C%20%27hierarchySemanticsExplicit%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-ONTOLOGY-MULTIPLE-LINK-ROOTS%27%2C%20%27multiple%20explicit%20ontology%20root%20links%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27An%20ontology%20can%20have%20several%20independently%20selectable%20roots%2C%20each%20represented%20as%20an%20explicit%20link%20in%20the%20global%20space.%20A%20root%20may%20also%20be%20a%20type%20only%20when%20its%20model%20declares%20that%20role%3B%20root%20selection%20and%20traversal%20retain%20identity%20and%20provenance.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27multipleOntologyRootsSelectable%27%2C%20%27ontologyRootsAreLinks%27%2C%20%27ontologyRootTypeRoleExplicit%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-TAXONOMY-MULTIPLE-LINK-ROOTS%27%2C%20%27multiple%20explicit%20taxonomy%20root%20links%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27A%20taxonomy%20can%20have%20several%20explicitly%20represented%20root%20links%20and%20multiple%20classification%20entry%20points.%20A%20root%20type%20role%20is%20declared%20by%20the%20selected%20model%20rather%20than%20inferred%20from%20being%20a%20root%2C%20and%20classification%20traversal%20preserves%20its%20declared%20semantics.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27multipleTaxonomyRootsSelectable%27%2C%20%27taxonomyRootsAreLinks%27%2C%20%27taxonomyRootTypeRoleExplicit%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%5D%29%2C%0A%20%20...rows%28%27linksFoundationRequest%27%2C%20linksSource%2C%20%27links-as-fundamental-entities-and-relationships%27%2C%20%27links-foundation%27%2C%20%5B%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-LINK-FOUNDATION-UNIVERSAL-REPRESENTATION%27%2C%20%27links%20as%20the%20fundamental%20representation%20of%20concepts%2C%20entities%20and%20relationships%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Every%20represented%20concept%2C%20entity%2C%20relationship%2C%20root%20and%20formal%20definition%20is%20fundamentally%20a%20link%20or%20composition%20of%20links%20in%20the%20same%20network.%20Independent%20host%20objects%20or%20hidden%20side%20tables%20cannot%20substitute%20for%20the%20common%20representation.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27conceptsEntitiesRelationshipsAreLinks%27%2C%20%27rootsAndDefinitionsAreLinks%27%2C%20%27noHiddenEntityRepresentation%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-LINK-FOUNDATION-SELF-LOOP-VERTEX%27%2C%20%27vertex%20represented%20by%20a%20self-referencing%20link%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27The%20selected%20links%20model%20can%20represent%20a%20vertex%20as%20a%20link%20whose%20beginning%20and%20end%20reference%20that%20same%20link.%20Its%20identity%2C%20self-reference%20and%20selected%20model%20are%20explicit%20and%20survive%20serialization%20and%20reload.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27selfLoopVertexRepresentable%27%2C%20%27selfReferencingEndpointsPreserved%27%2C%20%27vertexModelAndIdentityRetained%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-LINK-FOUNDATION-MULTIPLE-ROLES%27%2C%20%27one%20link%20as%20relationship%2C%20concept%20and%20entity%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27The%20same%20link%20can%20carry%20relationship%2C%20concept%20and%20entity%20roles%20without%20replacing%20its%20identity%20with%20disconnected%20host%20representations.%20Role%20declarations%20and%20multiple%20root%20selections%20remain%20inspectable%20links.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27linkIdentitySharedAcrossRoles%27%2C%20%27rolesAreExplicitLinks%27%2C%20%27multipleRootRolesPreserved%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-LINK-FOUNDATION-RECURSIVE-COMPOSITION%27%2C%20%27recursive%20compositional%20links%20across%20representation%20levels%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Links%20can%20reference%20and%20compose%20other%20links%20recursively%20across%20representation%20levels%2C%20preserving%20the%20reusable%20structural%20motif%2C%20shared%20references%20and%20explicit%20cycles.%20This%20compositional%20model%20does%20not%20itself%20establish%20a%20mathematical%20fractal%20dimension%20or%20eliminate%20logical%20paradoxes.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27recursiveLinkCompositionPreserved%27%2C%20%27sharedMotifAndCyclesExplicit%27%2C%20%27noUnprovedConsistencyInference%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-LINK-FOUNDATION-OPTIONAL-TYPE-ROOT%27%2C%20%27declared%20type%20roots%20without%20a%20universal%20self-typing%20axiom%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27A%20model%20may%20declare%20a%20root%20link%20to%20be%20a%20type.%20The%20representation%20does%20not%20infer%20a%20universal%20Type%3AType%20axiom%20or%20a%20universal%20proof%20logic%20from%20links%2C%20self-loops%2C%20recursion%20or%20root%20membership%3B%20foundation%20premises%20remain%20explicit%20and%20selectable.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27rootTypeRolesDeclared%27%2C%20%27noImplicitUniversalSelfTyping%27%2C%20%27selectedFoundationPremisesPreserved%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%5D%29%2C%0A%20%20...rows%28%27linksFoundationRequest%27%2C%20linksSource%2C%20%27links-as-fundamental-entities-and-relationships%27%2C%20%27links-foundation%27%2C%20%5B%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-LINK-FOUNDATION-PHYSICAL-ANALOGY%27%2C%20%27recorded%20wave%20and%20fractal%20motivation%20with%20an%20explicit%20epistemic%20boundary%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27The%20user%20wave%2C%20particle%20and%20fractal%20analogy%20is%20preserved%20verbatim%20as%20motivation%20and%20a%20hypothesis.%20Documentation%20and%20formal%20models%20do%20not%20report%20those%20physical%20propositions%2C%20universal%20self-similarity%20or%20freedom%20from%20contradictions%20as%20established%20facts%20or%20consistency%20proofs.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27physicalAnalogyCapturedVerbatim%27%2C%20%27physicalPropositionsMarkedAsHypotheses%27%2C%20%27noAnalogyPresentedAsConsistencyProof%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%5D%2C%20true%29%2C%0A%20%20...rows%28%27recordConversationRequest%27%2C%20recordingSource%2C%20%27critical-conversation-requirements%27%2C%20%27conversation-contract%27%2C%20%5B%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-CONVERSATION-VERBATIM-REGISTER%27%2C%20%27immutable%20hashed%20capture%20of%20every%20requirement-bearing%20conversation%20message%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Every%20requirement-bearing%20conversation%20message%20is%20captured%20verbatim%20with%20its%20content%20hash%20and%20explicit%20capture%20provenance%2C%20registered%20as%20a%20source%20and%20linked%20to%20atomic%20obligations.%20New%20messages%20append%20captures%20rather%20than%20overwriting%20earlier%20requests.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27conversationMessagesCapturedVerbatim%27%2C%20%27captureHashesVerified%27%2C%20%27allConversationObligationsMapped%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-CONVERSATION-CRITICAL-DELIVERY%27%2C%20%27critical%20classification%20of%20all%20conversation%20and%20inherited%20obligations%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Every%20conversation%20requirement%20and%20every%20inherited%20ledger%20obligation%20is%20critical%20and%20blocks%20a%20full-scope%20delivery%20or%20release-completion%20claim%20while%20it%20lacks%20required%20exact-commit%20evidence.%20Existing%20source%2C%20scope%2C%20assertions%2C%20fixtures%2C%20runtimes%20and%20checkpoint%20execution%20order%20remain%20intact.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27allRequirementsCritical%27%2C%20%27unverifiedRowsBlockFullScopeDelivery%27%2C%20%27inheritedScopeAndCheckpointsPreserved%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%5D%2C%20true%29%2C%0A%20%20...rows%28%27associativeFoundationRequest%27%2C%20stackSource%2C%20%27associative-stack-and-theoretical-foundation%27%2C%20%27associative-foundation%27%2C%20%5B%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-ASSOCIATIVE-STACK-PINNED-SOURCE-AUDIT%27%2C%20%27pinned%20audit%20of%20the%20referenced%20associative%20technology%20stack%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27The%20project%20audit%20reads%20the%20referenced%20formal-ai%20associative%20technology%20stack%20at%20a%20recorded%20immutable%20revision%20and%20records%20its%20content%20hash%2C%20providers%20and%20dependency-role%20boundaries.%20A%20moving%20main%20URL%20or%20a%20provider%20name%20alone%20does%20not%20establish%20adoption.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27associativeStackSourceReadAndPinned%27%2C%20%27stackContentHashRecorded%27%2C%20%27providerRolesClassified%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-ASSOCIATIVE-STACK-PROJECT-WIDE-USE%27%2C%20%27associative%20stack%20adoption%20across%20the%20entire%20project%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27An%20executable%20project-wide%20audit%20covers%20both%20packages%2C%20code%2C%20grammars%2C%20translation%2C%20tools%2C%20documentation%20and%20dependencies%20against%20the%20relevant%20associative%20stack%20obligations.%20Direct%20runtime%20providers%2C%20compatibility%20or%20theoretical%20alignment%20and%20development%20tools%20are%20distinguished%3B%20unrelated%20formal-ai%20dependencies%20are%20not%20blindly%20introduced.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27entireProjectStackUsageAudited%27%2C%20%27actualCodeAndDependenciesTraced%27%2C%20%27runtimeCompatibilityAndDevelopmentRolesDistinct%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-THEORY-FOUNDATION-PINNED-SOURCE-AUDIT%27%2C%20%27pinned%20philosophical%20and%20theoretical%20meta-theory%20foundation%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27The%20meta-theory%20source%20is%20read%20at%20an%20immutable%20revision%20with%20archived%20releases%20and%20drafts%20identified%20separately.%20Adopted%20definitions%2C%20assumptions%20and%20provenance%20are%20recorded%20explicitly%3B%20a%20repository%20citation%20alone%20is%20insufficient%20as%20a%20theoretical%20foundation.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27metaTheorySourceReadAndPinned%27%2C%20%27archivesAndDraftsDistinguished%27%2C%20%27adoptedDefinitionsAndAssumptionsTraced%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%5D%2C%20true%29%2C%0A%20%20...rows%28%27associativeFoundationRequest%27%2C%20stackSource%2C%20%27associative-stack-and-theoretical-foundation%27%2C%20%27associative-foundation%27%2C%20%5B%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-THEORY-FOUNDATION-PROJECT-WIDE-APPLICATION%27%2C%20%27meta-theory%20foundation%20applied%20to%20the%20common%20links%20model%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27The%20common%20concept%2C%20grammar%2C%20ontology%2C%20taxonomy%2C%20entity%20and%20relationship%20representation%20applies%20the%20adopted%20links%20meta-theory%20definitions%20throughout%20both%20packages.%20Model%20choices%2C%20theoretical%20premises%20and%20operational%20encodings%20remain%20explicit%20inspectable%20links%20with%20source%20provenance.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27metaTheoryDefinitionsAppliedProjectWide%27%2C%20%27modelPremisesAreInspectableLinks%27%2C%20%27operationalEncodingsRetainProvenance%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-THEORY-FOUNDATION-CONSUMER-BOUNDARIES%27%2C%20%27theoretical%20foundation%20separated%20from%20consumer%20proof%20authority%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27The%20shared%20philosophical%20and%20theoretical%20links%20foundation%20does%20not%20silently%20choose%20a%20universal%20proof%20logic%2C%20Type%3AType%20axiom%20or%20consumer%20execution%20policy.%20Consumer-owned%20logical%20semantics%20and%20proof%20authority%20remain%20separate%20explicit%20model%20choices%20with%20checked%20correspondences.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27theoreticalAndConsumerFoundationsDistinct%27%2C%20%27noSilentUniversalLogicOrSelfTyping%27%2C%20%27consumerProofAuthorityPreserved%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%5D%29%2C%0A%20%20...rows%28%27globalConceptSpace%27%2C%20originalSource%2C%20%27critical-conversation-requirements%27%2C%20%27workflow-contract%27%2C%20%5B%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-WORKFLOW-FAST-CONTINUOUS-PROGRESS%27%2C%20%27fast%20continuous%20implementation%20between%20bulk%20feedback%20cycles%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Deliver%20the%20complete%20authorized%20scope%20as%20quickly%20as%20available%20resources%20and%20correct%20verification%20permit%2C%20using%20useful%20parallel%20work%20and%20coherent%20batches.%20Continue%20independent%20drafting%20and%20implementation%20while%20CI%20runs%20instead%20of%20waiting%20idle%3B%20speed%20never%20substitutes%20for%20required%20behavior%20or%20evidence.%27%2C%20%5B%27independentWorkContinuesDuringCi%27%2C%20%27deliveryLatencyMinimizedWithoutScopeReduction%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-WORKFLOW-LATEST-REPOSITORY%27%2C%20%27latest%20repository%20version%20in%20the%20shared%20local%20checkout%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Before%20drafting%20the%20batch%2C%20the%20coordinator%20obtains%20the%20latest%20authorized%20repository%20and%20pull-request%20refs%2C%20reconciles%20required%20main%20changes%20and%20records%20the%20checkout%20revision%20used%20for%20implementation%20and%20CI%20feedback.%27%2C%20%5B%27latestAuthorizedRefsObtained%27%2C%20%27checkoutRevisionRecorded%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-WORKFLOW-BULK-EXACT-SCOPE%27%2C%20%27one%20bulk%20draft%20of%20exactly%20all%20issue%2C%20pull-request%20and%20conversation%20obligations%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Bulk%20work%20covers%20every%20registered%20issue%2C%20pull-request%20and%20conversation%20obligation%2C%20preserving%20all%20inherited%20scope.%20Drafting%2C%20implementation%20and%20reporting%20do%20not%20substitute%20narrower%20capabilities%20or%20omit%20unresolved%20requirements.%27%2C%20%5B%27entireRegisteredScopeIncluded%27%2C%20%27noScopeSubstitutionOrOmission%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-WORKFLOW-MINIMAL-LOCAL-RESOURCES%27%2C%20%27minimal%20local%20resources%20and%20targeted%20JavaScript%20validation%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Local%20work%20uses%20the%20minimum%20resources%20needed%20for%20targeted%20JavaScript%20validation%20and%20authoring.%20Full%20suites%2C%20whole-registry%20experiments%2C%20downstream%20workload%20clones%20and%20native%20toolchain%20matrices%20remain%20CI%20work.%27%2C%20%5B%27targetedJavaScriptOnlyLocally%27%2C%20%27expensiveChecksDelegatedToCI%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-WORKFLOW-PARALLEL-DELEGATION%27%2C%20%27maximum%20useful%20independent%20agent%20delegation%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Independent%20bulk%20tasks%20are%20split%20among%20as%20many%20useful%20authorized%20agents%20as%20the%20available%20concurrency%20permits%2C%20with%20clear%20ownership%20and%20integration%20coordination%20over%20the%20shared%20checkout.%27%2C%20%5B%27independentTasksDelegated%27%2C%20%27availableConcurrencyUsedWithOwnership%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-WORKFLOW-CONTRIBUTOR-COMMITS%27%2C%20%27every%20contributor%20commits%20its%20reviewable%20work%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Every%20contributor%20with%20implementation%20work%20commits%20its%20explicit%20owned%20paths%2C%20preserving%20other%20agents%20staged%20changes%20and%20retaining%20reviewable%20commit%20provenance%20for%20the%20bulk%20batch.%27%2C%20%5B%27everyContributorWorkCommitted%27%2C%20%27ownedPathsAndCommitProvenanceRetained%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-WORKFLOW-SINGLE-PUSH-COORDINATOR%27%2C%20%27one%20coordinator%20performs%20batch%20pushes%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Exactly%20one%20authorized%20coordinator%20pushes%20the%20integrated%20batch%20after%20reviewing%20all%20committed%20work.%20Other%20contributors%20commit%20their%20changes%20without%20pushing.%27%2C%20%5B%27singlePushCoordinatorEnforced%27%2C%20%27integratedBatchReviewedBeforePush%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-WORKFLOW-PREVIOUS-CI-TERMINAL%27%2C%20%27previous%20CI%20fully%20finished%20before%20a%20new%20batch%20push%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Before%20pushing%20the%20next%20integrated%20batch%2C%20the%20coordinator%20verifies%20the%20prior%20relevant%20CI%2FCD%20runs%20are%20fully%20finished%20and%20inspects%20their%20complete%20failure%20feedback.%20The%20batch%20has%20new%20concrete%20requirements%20or%20fixes%20to%20deliver.%27%2C%20%5B%27previousCiRunsTerminal%27%2C%20%27completeFeedbackInspected%27%2C%20%27newConcreteBatchChangesPresent%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-WORKFLOW-PREVIOUS-CI-ERRORS-ADDRESSED%27%2C%20%27all%20previous%20CI%20errors%20addressed%20before%20the%20feedback%20push%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Every%20prior%20CI%2FCD%20error%20is%20addressed%20with%20concrete%20implementation%20and%20the%20applicable%20targeted%20verification%20before%20the%20integrated%20feedback%20push.%20No%20failing%20check%20is%20described%20as%20intended%20and%20no%20acceptance%20gate%20is%20weakened.%27%2C%20%5B%27allPreviousCiErrorsAddressed%27%2C%20%27targetedFixVerificationRecorded%27%2C%20%27gatesRemainIntact%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-WORKFLOW-NO-LOCAL-RUST-COMPILATION%27%2C%20%27no%20local%20Rust%20compilation%20during%20the%20requested%20workflow%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27No%20contributor%20compiles%20Rust%20locally%20for%20testing%20in%20this%20workflow.%20JavaScript%20validation%20develops%20the%20system%20behavior%2C%20and%20compiled%20Rust%20parity%2C%20platform%20and%20native%20execution%20checks%20run%20in%20CI.%27%2C%20%5B%27noRustCompiledLocally%27%2C%20%27rustExecutionChecksRunInCI%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-WORKFLOW-AUTOMATED-TRANSLATION%27%2C%20%27JavaScript-first%20automated%20translation%20and%20referenced%20best%20practices%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Bulk%20work%20develops%20JavaScript%20behavior%20first%2C%20ports%20through%20automated%20translation%20where%20supported%20and%20applies%20the%20relevant%20pinned%20practices%20from%20Router%20PR761%2C%20formal-ai%20PR1188%20and%20Relative%20Meta%20Logic%20PR184.%20Unsupported%20translation%20constructs%20remain%20implementation%20gaps%20rather%20than%20hand-written%20substitutes%20or%20success%20declarations.%27%2C%20%5B%27javascriptFirstBulkDevelopment%27%2C%20%27automatedTranslationUsed%27%2C%20%27referencedPracticesAudited%27%2C%20%27unsupportedTranslationGapsRetained%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%5D%2C%20true%29%2C%0A%20%20...rows%28%22recursiveConcreteSyntaxRequest%22%2C%20%22parity%2Fsources%2Frecursive-concrete-syntax-and-any-grammar-2026-10-16.txt%22%2C%20%22concrete-and-abstract-syntax-trees%22%2C%20%22recursive-concrete-syntax%22%2C%20%5B%0A%